00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.190
Speaker 1: Yes, that's exactly it.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.630
This is a great question, which is for a long
time, Republicans have been saying they haven't

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.960
so much been saying the hospitalization numbers
are exaggerated.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.380
Republicans have been saying the death numbers
are being exaggerated.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.020
And at one point they were saying hospitals
lie and say someone died from COVID to get

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.020
more money.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.020
Now we debunked that.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:27.340
What is true is that if someone is in the
hospital for COVID on average, it's more expensive

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.380
to treat them than when someone does not have
COVID.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.810
So it doesn't matter if they die or not.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:38.320
Medicare reimburses more money if someone
actually is treated for COVID, because on

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.810
average, that's more expensive to treat.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:47.460
The difference is, before there was no data
that pointed to a ton of the people in the

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:54.940
hospital, with COVID being in the hospital
for something else before you had a situation

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.490
Speaker 2: where
Speaker 1: almost anything that was elective

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.040
or non-emergency was shut down.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:09.140
The hospitalization rate for the earlier strains
was higher, and there was no data that suggested

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.459
many of the people hospitalized right now
with COVID are actually here for something

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:14.459
else.

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:21.519
We now have actual data, including, for example,
from New York City and Akron is so contagious

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:27.909
it is so widespread and it is also asymptomatic
and so many people that in New York City.

00:02:27.909 --> 00:02:34.980
Half of those in the hospital with COVID were
not in the hospital because of COVID.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.909
They are not being treated with COVID.

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:40.090
They, incidentally, are positive, but they're
there for something else.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:46.299
So the reason why we now can say that and
before we couldn't is that the data actually

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.540
reflects that.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.870
It's a perfectly fair question.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:50.870
And that's the answer.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.579
And they're exactly the types of questions
that we should be asking.

